From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:44:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] Treat clang's mingw-w64 TLS as native

wscript defines MINGW_NATIVE_TLS, which routes access to the
thread_local Temporal::TempoMap::_tempo_map_p through an exported
accessor, only when `$CC -v` reports a GCC configured with --enable-tls.
Clang targeting mingw-w64 always uses native TLS (no emutls), but its
-v output has no such configure line, so the inline TempoMap::use()/
fetch() reference the TLS variable across the DLL boundary and lld
fails:

  ld.lld: error: unable to automatically import from
  _ZN8Temporal8TempoMap12_tempo_map_pE with relocation type
  IMAGE_REL_AMD64_SECREL in libs/ardour/async_midi_port.cc.1.o

Enable MINGW_NATIVE_TLS for clang as well.
---
 wscript | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wscript b/wscript
index e38fe01..87a6804 100644
--- a/wscript
+++ b/wscript
@@ -1284,6 +1284,9 @@ int main () { return 0; }
         # gcc -v prints configure flags to stderr, not stdout
         gcc_config = subprocess.run([str(conf.env['CC'][0]), '-v'], capture_output=True, text=True).stderr
         have_native_tls = '--enable-tls' in gcc_config
+        # clang does not use emutls for mingw-w64 targets; its TLS is always native
+        if 'clang version' in gcc_config:
+            have_native_tls = True
 
         if have_native_tls:
             conf.env.append_value('CFLAGS', '-DMINGW_NATIVE_TLS')
